Third-party code and libraries
------------------------------

palette 0.7 (dev-dependency, tests only)
  https://github.com/Ogeon/palette
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Used as an independent check of the IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB transfer. The
  runtime curve lives in kagra-shared/src/render/color_space.rs and the
  WGSL shaders so the wasm and Android builds do not link this crate.

image 0.25 (jpeg and webp features only; default features off so rayon stays out)
  https://github.com/image-rs/image
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Decodes glTF JPEG (via zune-jpeg) and WebP (via image-webp). PNG stays
  on the png crate. The wasm and Android builds use these pure-Rust
  decoders.

image-webp (pulled by image's webp feature)
  https://github.com/image-rs/image-webp
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Lossless and lossy WebP decode for glTF images. No encoder in the runtime.

ktx2 0.5
  https://github.com/BVE-Reborn/ktx2
  Apache-2.0
  Reads a KTX2 container. The runtime uploads pre-encoded ETC2, ASTC, and
  BC color blocks when the adapter lists the matching compression feature.
  Basis Universal and supercompression are rejected. There is no encoder
  and no transcoder.

The Narkowicz ACES fit in bloom.wgsl and shader3d.wgsl is the public
approximation published by Krzysztof Narkowicz (2016), used widely
including by three.js (MIT). No three.js source is copied in this tree.

The AgX inset and outset matrices in color_space.rs, bloom.wgsl, and
shader3d.wgsl are Troy Sobotka's AgX base
(https://github.com/sobotka/AgX, public domain). The log2 / smoothstep
between those matrices is original. Not a copy of three.js AgXToneMapping.

Khronos PBR Neutral in the same files follows the published curve
(https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ToneMapping, Apache-2.0). The
implementation is original. The sky atmosphere is a short Rayleigh / Mie
mix written here. No three.js Sky shader is copied.

The post pass graph (kagra-shared/src/render/post.rs, post.wgsl) follows
the shape of three.js EffectComposer / ShaderPass and the ideas in
SSAOShader, BokehPass, and the Karis neighborhood clamp used by TAA
examples (three.js, MIT, https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js). The WGSL
is original. No three.js source is copied.

Cascade selection follows the parallel-split idea used by three.js
CSM (MIT, https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js). The rings here are fixed
concentric extents packed into one 2048 map: count 3 is 8 / 24 / 80 m,
count 2 is 8 / 80 m, count 1 stays the historical 24 m tile. Not
three.js frustum-slice practical splits. No three.js source is copied.

The 8-bit bloom mip chain follows three.js UnrealBloomPass (MIT,
https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js): a luma high-pass, then downsample
and additive upsample. The WGSL in bloom_ldr.wgsl is original. No
three.js source is copied.

The procedural SFX in kagra-shared/src/sfx.rs follow the shape of sfxr
(Tomas Pettersson / DrPetter, MIT, http://www.drpetter.se/project_sfxr.html):
a waveform, a pitch slide, and a decay. The oscillator and the preset
numbers are original. No sfxr source is copied. Wasm calls `synthWav`.

rapier3d 0.35
  https://github.com/dimforge/rapier
  Apache-2.0
  Rigid bodies, and `KinematicCharacterController` for
  `PhysicsWorld::move_character` (slide, snap, autostep). The wasm
  build keeps parry's default SIMD off. No Rapier source is copied.

simple-easing 1.1.1
  https://gitlab.com/chpio/simple-easing
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Named easing curves for kagra_shared::juice. No source is copied
  into this tree. kagra/juice.py keeps the same curve names in pure
  Python so tests do not import the extension.

Point sprites follow the idea of three.js Points, and fat lines follow
Line2 (MIT, https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js): a camera-facing quad
per point, and a clip-space quad per segment whose width is in pixels.
The WGSL in strokes.wgsl is original. No three.js source is copied.
WebGPU point-list stays unused (it is one pixel). No storage buffers.

puffin 0.19
  https://github.com/emilk/puffin
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  CPU scopes for a frame and a sim tick. The puffin_http viewer is not
  a dependency. Timestamp queries stay off wasm.

notify 6 (desktop only; not linked on wasm or Android)
  https://github.com/notify-rs/notify
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Watches a world dump and its material files so the desktop window can reload them.
